# Chapter: signed firmware updates over Bluetooth.
#
# Settings > Information > Bluetooth Link, then the hand-over to the update screen when the phone
# asks for update mode, a transfer with its progress, and the verified restart. The other end of the
# link does not exist on the host, so the scene scripts what the display would report: the
# companion and update fixtures stand in for the phone, and the progress is a time-lapse of a
# transfer that takes minutes on a real display. Every screen is the firmware's own.
title "Updates over Bluetooth"
subtitle "Signed, checked before anything is erased, and safe to interrupt."
note "The phone and the radio are not simulated. The screens are the firmware's own and the transfer is scripted."

# A release build: the signing key is present, so update mode is available.
update ready
companion advertising seconds=48
demo 1
boot dashboard

wait 1000
caption "Never while riding" "The display offers an update only while Bluetooth Link is open: Settings, then Information."
tap 160 120 settle=600
tap-label "SETTINGS" settle=600
tap-label "INFO" settle=1500
tap-label "BLUETOOTH LINK" settle=1800

caption "A short window" "Open KAJO Companion on a phone, or the Windows uploader, and connect."
wait 1800
companion connected seconds=287
caption "Riding data carries on" "A wired controller keeps reporting. A Bluetooth one is let go while the link is open."
wait 2800

caption "The phone asks" "It requests update mode. The display stops ride logging and takes over."
update-request
wait 1500
update advertising
wait 1300
update connected
caption "Signed images only" "The release is signed with an offline key. The display checks the signature before it erases anything."
wait 3000

update receiving
caption "A spare slot" "Two firmware slots. The new image is written to the one you are not running."
update-progress 35 3200
caption "Sector by sector" "Each compressed sector is checked, written once and acknowledged. A dropped link resumes where it stopped."
update-progress 78 3200
update-progress 100 1800
caption "Verified" "The image is hashed and checked, then the display restarts by itself in five seconds."
update ready-to-reboot
wait 2800

caption "Rollback-safe" "The new firmware has ten seconds of healthy running to confirm itself, or the bootloader goes back to the old one."
wait 3600

caption "Older releases ask first" "A signed downgrade waits for a tap on the display."
update confirm-downgrade
wait 3000
tap-label "CANCEL" settle=600
update cancelled received=0
wait 2600
